  "14": {
    "frame": 100,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_11",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Thomas Hobbes, at your service. Without a sovereign, life is solitary, poor, nasty, brutish, and short.",
            "You think you can argue for a state of nature? Let us see."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "hobbes"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Perhaps the Leviathan need not be so absolute after all.",
            "But beware — without order, chaos returns."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "15": {
    "frame": 110,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_12",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "David Hume here. Reason is, and ought only to be, the slave of the passions.",
            "Can you show me that morality is more than sentiment? I rather doubt it."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "hume"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "A most engaging exchange. But I remain skeptical that reason alone can move us to act.",
            "The is-ought gap yawns as wide as ever."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "16": {
    "frame": 120,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_13",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "G.E. Moore. I put it to you: goodness is a simple, indefinable quality.",
            "Any attempt to define it commits the naturalistic fallacy. Shall we discuss?"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "moore"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Your open question was... surprisingly persuasive.",
            "Perhaps the relationship between natural and moral properties is more complex than I supposed."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "17": {
    "frame": 130,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_14",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "I am A.J. Ayer. Moral statements are neither true nor false — they are mere expressions of emotion.",
            "If you disagree, you are simply expressing a different attitude. Shall we test this?"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "ayer"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Boo! Hurrah! ...I concede your argument had more substance than mere attitude.",
            "Perhaps the verification principle needs revision."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "18": {
    "frame": 140,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_15",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Elizabeth Anscombe. Modern moral philosophy is bankrupt without an adequate philosophy of psychology.",
            "You cannot understand obligation without understanding intention. Prove me wrong."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "anscombe"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You argue with genuine intention — I will grant you that.",
            "But the question of what grounds 'ought' remains open."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "19": {
    "frame": 70,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_8",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Bernard Williams. Moral philosophy has been distorted by its obsession with obligation.",
            "Thick ethical concepts, agent-relative reasons, moral luck — these are what matter. Ready?"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "williams"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "One thought too many? Perhaps. But you gave me just enough to reconsider.",
            "Ethics and the limits of philosophy... indeed."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "20": {
    "frame": 12,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_2",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Hey! Morality is just whatever your culture says it is!",
            "You think YOUR values are better than anyone else's? How arrogant!"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "cultural_relativist"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Okay, maybe the fact that cultures differ doesn't prove no one is wrong...",
            "I've got some reading to do."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "21": {
    "frame": 22,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_3",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Morality? It's all just feelings, man. There's nothing to argue about.",
            "You say 'wrong,' I say 'boo.' Same thing."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "unreflective_emotivist"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Huh. I guess saying 'it's all just feelings' is itself a claim that needs defending.",
            "Maybe I should actually read Ayer before quoting him..."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "22": {
    "frame": 32,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_4",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Simple math! More happiness equals more good. What's so hard about that?",
            "Rights, duties, virtues -- they're all just obstacles to maximizing utility!"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "naive_utilitarian"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Okay, maybe you can't just put happiness on a spreadsheet...",
            "Mill did say something about 'higher pleasures.' Maybe I should read past the first chapter."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "23": {
    "frame": 42,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_5",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Let me guess -- you think people actually care about others? Please.",
            "Everything anyone does is for themselves. I'm just honest about it."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "crude_egoist"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "If my theory can explain literally everything, maybe it doesn't actually explain anything...",
            "I think I confused 'having a motive' with 'being selfish.' Those aren't the same, are they?"
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "24": {
    "frame": 52,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_6",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Justice? Fairness? Those are just pretty words the weak use to hold back the strong.",
            "Power is the only thing that matters in this world. Want me to prove it?"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "might_makes_right"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You beat me with arguments, not force. I... don't know what to do with that.",
            "Maybe Thrasymachus was wrong. Socrates did have something on him."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "25": {
    "frame": 62,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_7",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You didn't choose to stop and talk to me. Physics chose for you.",
            "Free will is an illusion. Nothing you do matters, morally speaking."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "simple_determinist"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Was I determined to lose this argument? That's... actually a weird thought.",
            "Maybe responsibility doesn't require some magical free will. I need to think harder about this."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "26": {
    "frame": 72,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_8",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Morality comes from divine command. End of discussion.",
            "Without God, anything is permitted. You have no foundation!"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "dogmatic_divine_commander"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Is something good because God commands it, or does God command it because it's good?",
            "That question... I never let myself ask it before. Maybe I should."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "27": {
    "frame": 82,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_9",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Everyone knows what's right and wrong. It's obvious.",
            "You philosophers just overcomplicate everything with your fancy arguments!"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "crude_moral_realist"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Okay, 'everyone knows' isn't actually an argument, is it...",
            "Maybe understanding WHY things are right matters as much as knowing THAT they are."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "28": {
    "frame": 20,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_3",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "No rule or principle can tell you what to do here.",
            "You must see what the situation requires. That is phronesis."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "mcdowell"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You saw what the situation demanded without reaching for a rule.",
            "That perceptual sensitivity is the beginning of practical wisdom."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "29": {
    "frame": 50,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_6",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Imagine a person devoted entirely to moral perfection.",
            "Would you actually want to spend time with them? I think not."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "wolf"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You showed that moral seriousness and a rich life can coexist.",
            "Perhaps the moral saint could learn something from you after all."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "30": {
    "frame": 20,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_3",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Moral life cannot be reduced to a single principle.",
            "The good, the right, and the virtuous pull in different directions."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "dewey"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You respected the complexity of moral experience.",
            "That is no small achievement where others would simplify."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "31": {
    "frame": 30,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_4",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "When you say something is 'good,' you express an attitude.",
            "But there is more to it than Ayer admits. Let me show you."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "stevenson"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Your words carried both descriptive truth and emotive force.",
            "I find my attitudes... genuinely shifted."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "32": {
    "frame": 10,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_2",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Aristotle. I walk this colonnade because virtue is a practice, not a theorem.",
            "Walk with me, then, and defend your account of the good life."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "aristotle"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "One debate does not make a philosopher, any more than one swallow makes a spring.",
            "But you argued well. Keep practicing."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "33": {
    "frame": 80,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_9",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Jeremy Bentham. Pleasure and pain are the only coins this stall accepts.",
            "State your position and I will run the calculus on it."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "bentham"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "The sum came out in your favor this time.",
            "Nonsense upon stilts it was not."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "34": {
    "frame": 90,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_10",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "John Stuart Mill. Better a Socrates dissatisfied than a fool satisfied.",
            "Which are you? Argue with me and we shall find out."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "mill"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "He who knows only his own side of the case knows little of that.",
            "You clearly know mine. I concede the exchange."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "35": {
    "frame": 40,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_5",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Philippa Foot. Moral evaluation is no more mysterious than calling a root system good or bad.",
            "A runaway trolley is heading for five people. Shall we begin?"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "foot"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You kept your grip on the difference between doing and allowing.",
            "That is rarer than it should be."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "36": {
    "frame": 50,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_6",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "P.F. Strawson. Resentment, gratitude, indignation: our practices need no metaphysical license.",
            "Convince me that determinism should change how we hold one another responsible."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "strawson"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "I find myself feeling something like gratitude.",
            "How fitting that the reactive attitudes should have the last word."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "37": {
    "frame": 80,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_9",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Donald Davidson. To interpret you at all I must assume you are mostly rational.",
            "Test that charity. Give me your best argument."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "davidson"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Your reasons were causes, and good ones.",
            "Charity was the right policy after all."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "38": {
    "frame": 90,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_10",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Ronald Dworkin. There are right answers in morality, and skepticism is just another moral position.",
            "Defend yours, and I will hold it to the standard of integrity."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "dworkin"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You interpreted the argument in its best light and still made it your own.",
            "That is what taking rights seriously looks like."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "39": {
    "frame": 30,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_4",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "David Wiggins. Values are neither found ready-made in the world nor invented from nothing.",
            "Tell me what solidarity with human needs demands, and defend it."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "wiggins"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You matched the concept to the response it merits.",
            "A sensible subjectivist could ask no more."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "40": {
    "frame": 40,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_5",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Thomas Nagel. Step back far enough and your life looks absurd from nowhere.",
            "Now step back in and argue with me anyway."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "nagel"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "From the objective standpoint your victory means nothing.",
            "From here, however, it was well earned."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "41": {
    "frame": 80,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_9",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Sharon Street. Evolution shaped your moral intuitions with no eye on the truth.",
            "So why trust them? Defend your realism if you can."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "street"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Selected for or not, that was a fine piece of reasoning.",
            "The Darwinian dilemma will be waiting when you return."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "42": {
    "frame": 90,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_10",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "W.D. Ross. Fidelity, gratitude, non-maleficence: duties that no single principle can absorb.",
            "Show me how you weigh them when they conflict."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "ross"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Your judgment of where the greater duty lay was sound.",
            "That weighing is all our knowledge of the right amounts to."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "43": {
    "frame": 20,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_3",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "John Rawls. Imagine you did not know who in society you would be.",
            "What principles would you choose behind that veil? Defend them."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "rawls"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Your argument would be chosen in the original position.",
            "I can offer no higher compliment."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "44": {
    "frame": 30,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_4",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Robert Nozick. Individuals have rights, and there are things no one may do to them.",
            "Not even for the best of outcomes. Care to argue otherwise?"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "nozick"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You acquired that victory justly, so it is yours.",
            "I will not redistribute it."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "45": {
    "frame": 40,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_5",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Virginia Held. Morality did not begin with contracts between strangers but with the labor of care.",
            "Argue from your abstractions; I will answer from relations that sustain life."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "held"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You argued with attentiveness as well as rigor.",
            "Care and justice need not be rivals in you."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "46": {
    "frame": 90,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_10",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Rae Langton. Words do not merely describe the world; they rank, silence, and subordinate.",
            "So mind what your argument does, not just what it says. Begin."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "langton"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Your speech act came off: authority, uptake, and all.",
            "Use that power carefully."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "47": {
    "frame": 80,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_9",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Onora O'Neill. Could everyone act on the principle you are about to defend?",
            "If not, we will discover it together. Proceed."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "oneill"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Your maxim universalizes; I checked.",
            "Principles that others could follow are the only ones worth having."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "48": {
    "frame": 50,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_6",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Judith Jarvis Thomson. You wake up plugged into a famous violinist who needs your kidneys.",
            "May you unplug? Your answer will tell me everything. Let us debate."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "thomson"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You handled the case on its details instead of forcing a theory onto it.",
            "That is how the work actually gets done."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "49": {
    "frame": 30,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_4",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Michele Moody-Adams. No culture is so sealed off that its members cannot question its wrongs.",
            "Appeals to upbringing excuse nothing. Defend your view."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "moody_adams"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You took moral experience seriously without surrendering judgment.",
            "That balance is the real fieldwork of ethics."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "50": {
    "frame": 40,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_5",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Stephen Gardiner. Watch the tide: dispersed causes, distant victims, institutions that shrug.",
            "A perfect moral storm. Show me your ethics can weather it."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "gardiner"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "You resisted the temptation to corrupt the argument in your own favor.",
            "Against this storm, that is the rarest virtue."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "51": {
    "frame": 20,
    "animationKeyPrefix": "NPC_3",
    "events": [
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "J. David Velleman. Action is not mere behavior; it is behavior you can stand behind and narrate.",
            "So tell me the story of your view, and make it intelligible."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_NOT_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "DEBATE",
        "data": {
          "philosopherId": "velleman"
        }
      },
      {
        "requires": ["TRAINER_DEFEATED"],
        "type": "MESSAGE",
        "data": {
          "messages": [
            "Your argument made sense of itself as it went.",
            "That narrative unity is what agency amounts to."
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
